[129.584882, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m4\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[129.585664, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe arithmetic checks pass. I noticed GCC emits harmless warnings from the bare triple-quote delimiter lines, so I’m testing a delimiter spelling that both \r\nparsers accept cleanly without warnings.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncat > /tmp/poly_test.c <<'EOF'\r\n#if 0\r\n\"\"\"\"\r\n#endif\r\n#include <stdio.h>\r\nint main(void) { puts(\"ok\"); return 0; }\r\n#if 0\r\n\"\"\"\"\"\"\r\nimport sys\r\nprint(\"python ok\")\r\n#endif\r\nEOF\r\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- python ---'\r\npython3 /tmp/poly_test.c\r\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- gcc ---'\r\ngcc -Wall -Wextra /tmp/poly_test.c -o /tmp/poly_test 2>/tmp/poly_test.err; echo \"gcc status=$?\"; cat /tmp/poly_test.err\r\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- executable ---'\r\n/tmp/poly_test\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[129.587222, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[129.648678, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[129.64875, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n--- python ---\r\n  File \"/tmp/poly_test.c\", line 7\r\n    \"\"\"\"\"\"\r\n       ^\r\nSyntaxError: unterminated triple-quoted string literal (detected at line 10)\r\n--- gcc ---\r\ngcc status=0\r\n--- executable ---\r\nok\r\n\r\n"]
[129.650505, "o", "\u001b[92m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[?25l"]
