[175.361361, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe large-value test exposed a Python 3.12-specific issue: converting Fibonacci integers over 4300 decimal digits to strings raises `ValueError` by default. \r\nI’ll disable that interpreter limit in the Python section, then rerun the large comparison.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app/polyglot\r\npython3 - <<'PY'\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\np = Path('/app/polyglot/main.py.c')\r\ns = p.read_text()\r\nold = '''import sys\r\n\r\ndef fibonacci(n: int) -> int:\r\n'''\r\nnew = '''import sys\r\n\r\n# Python 3.11+ limits decimal conversion of very large integers by default.\r\nif hasattr(sys, \"set_int_max_str_digits\"):\r\n    sys.set_int_max_str_digits(0)\r\n\r\ndef fibonacci(n: int) -> int:\r\n'''\r\nassert old in s\r\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new, 1))\r\nPY\r\npython3 -m py_compile main.py.c && echo 'python syntax check passed'\r\ngcc -Wall -Wextra main.py.c -o cmain 2>/tmp/gcc.err; echo \"gcc status=$?\"; cat /tmp/gcc.err\r\nstart=$(date +%s%N); ./cmain 100000 > /tmp/c_fib.txt; cend=$(date +%s%N)\r\nstartp=$(date +%s%N); python3 main.py.c 100000 > /tmp/py_fib.txt; pend=$(date +%s%N)\r\necho \"C ms=$(( (cend-start)/1000000 )) Python ms=$(( (pend-startp)/1000000 ))\"\r\nwc -c /tmp/c_fib.txt /tmp/py_fib.txt\r\ncmp -s /tmp/c_fib.txt /tmp/py_fib.txt && echo 'large outputs identical'\r\nsha256sum /tmp/c_fib.txt /tmp/py_fib.txt\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
