[188.975063, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m12\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[188.975393, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe implementation is complete and verified: the same file runs under Python, compiles cleanly with GCC, and produces matching arbitrary-precision Fibonacci \r\nresults in both modes. I cleaned up generated binaries so the deliverable is the single requested source file.\r\n\r\n```\r\necho COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
